<rss version="0.92"><channel><item>
            <title>[LU-21245] OI scrub thread sleeps in D state and trips the hung task detector</title>
                <link>https://jira.whamcloud.com/browse/LU-21245</link>
                <project id="10000" key="LU">Lustre</project>
                    <description>&lt;p&gt;The OI scrub kthread throttles itself and waits for the LFSCK consumer with &lt;tt&gt;wait_var_event()&lt;/tt&gt;, which sleeps in TASK_UNINTERRUPTIBLE. When the consumer stalls for a while, e.g. while OSTs are unreachable after an MDS failover, the idle scrub thread stays in D state longer than &lt;tt&gt;hung_task_timeout_secs&lt;/tt&gt;. khungtaskd then reports it, and a node with &lt;tt&gt;kernel.hung_task_panic&lt;/tt&gt; set panics:&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;div class="preformatted panel" style="border-width: 1px;"&gt;&lt;div class="preformattedContent panelContent"&gt;
&lt;pre&gt;INFO: task OI_scrub:2637226 blocked for more than 122 seconds.
task:OI_scrub        state:D stack:0     pid:2637226 tgid:2637226 ppid:2      flags:0x00004000
Call Trace:
 __schedule+0x231/0x540
 schedule+0x2c/0xb0
 osd_scrub_next.constprop.0+0x2fe/0x9e0 [osd_zfs]
 osd_scrub_main+0x738/0xc40 [osd_zfs]
 kthread+0x101/0x110
 ret_from_fork+0x28/0x50
&lt;/pre&gt;
&lt;/div&gt;&lt;/div&gt;

&lt;p&gt;The trace is from osd-zfs during failover stress testing. osd-ldiskfs waits the same way in &lt;tt&gt;osd_scrub_exec()&lt;/tt&gt;, &lt;tt&gt;osd_inode_iteration()&lt;/tt&gt; and &lt;tt&gt;osd_scrub_main()&lt;/tt&gt;.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;These are idle waits: nothing is stuck while the consumer catches up. Sleeping in TASK_IDLE instead, with a TASK_IDLE variant of &lt;tt&gt;wait_var_event()&lt;/tt&gt;, keeps khungtaskd quiet and leaves the wakeup logic as it is.&lt;/p&gt;</description>
